 "measures": [
  {
   "name": "Public Measure US (Van Buren County Community School District)",
   "jurisdiction": "Van Buren County Community School District - only the Van Buren CSD splits of Cedar, Harrison and Van Buren townships (ballot styles CE-VB, HR-VB, VB-VB)",
   "ballotLanguage": "Shall the Board of Directors of the Van Buren County Community School District in the Counties of Van Buren, Davis, Henry and Lee, State of Iowa, be authorized to issue approximately $13,800,000 School Infrastructure Sales, Services and Use Tax Revenue and Refunding Bonds, which may be issued in one or more series over multiple fiscal years pursuant to Iowa Code Section 423F.2 and 423E.5, in the approximate amount of $13,800,000 for the purpose of providing funds to build, furnish, and equip an addition to the Keosauqua campus, including a secure entrance, classrooms, commons, and office space, and to improve the site; and to currently refund the outstanding School Infrastructure Sales, Services and Use Tax Revenue Bonds, Series 2022A, dated July 15, 2022, including costs of issuance and a debt service reserve fund if required by the purchaser; with any bond proceeds remaining after completion of this project used for other school infrastructure projects as authorized by the School District's Revenue Purpose Statement?"
  }
 ],
 "notes": "COMPLETE. Source: Lee County Auditor's official 2026 General Election sample ballot book (all 39 ballot styles, 78 pages, text PDF; opened in a real browser, then downloaded directly) cross-checked with the official Notice of General Election. Supervisors are elected by district (only Districts 2 and 3 up). District 2 (Greenwald D / Schulz R): Fort Madison FM1, FM2, FM3, FM4B. District 3 (Seeley R): FM4A, FM5 (city, Jefferson Twp and Madison Twp splits), the Cedar/Charleston/Harrison/Van Buren precinct (all its township, Houghton city and Van Buren CSD splits) and the Jefferson/West Montrose precinct. Keokuk (KE1-KE7), Des Moines/Jackson, East Montrose/Montrose city, Green Bay/Denmark/Pleasant Ridge, Marion/Franklin/Donnellson-Franklin-St. Paul, West Point and Washington styles have no supervisor contest. Vote-for counts from the ballots: SWCD vote for two; Ag Extension vote for five; every township trustee (incl. To Fill A Vacancy) and clerk is vote for one. Contests with no printed candidate (Charleston Twp Trustee and Trustee-vacancy, Denmark Twp Trustee-vacancy, Franklin Twp Trustee and Clerk, Montrose Twp Clerk, Pleasant Ridge Twp Trustee, West Point Twp Clerk and Trustee-vacancy) are write-in only. Montrose Township contests appear on both East Montrose and West Montrose styles; Jefferson Township contests on FM5-Jefferson and Jefferson/West Montrose styles. Public Measure US (Van Buren County CSD) appears only on the CE-VB, HR-VB and VB-VB styles. No other county or local measures. Party labels from the ballot."
}